1
00:00:00,680 --> 00:00:03,373
On October eighteenth, twenty twenty six,

2
00:00:03,393 --> 00:00:07,443
an armored vehicle drove past a village called Santo,

3
00:00:07,463 --> 00:00:09,705
east of Port au Prince.

4
00:00:09,725 --> 00:00:13,775
Inside were four technicians from El Salvador's Air Force.

5
00:00:15,095 --> 00:00:18,521
Gunmen attacked. According to El Salvador's armed forces,

6
00:00:18,541 --> 00:00:22,398
explosives were used, and the vehicle was set on

7
00:00:22,418 --> 00:00:24,982
fire. The four men got out.

8
00:00:25,002 --> 00:00:26,705
Then they were taken.

9
00:00:28,025 --> 00:00:31,286
Three days later, the president of El Salvador made

10
00:00:31,306 --> 00:00:34,566
a promise. If his men were not brought back

11
00:00:34,586 --> 00:00:36,753
alive, he would finish Haiti's gangs,

12
00:00:36,773 --> 00:00:39,669
the way he says he finished his own.

13
00:00:40,989 --> 00:00:44,663
Within a week, his government said two thousand Salvadoran

14
00:00:44,683 --> 00:00:46,305
soldiers were in Haiti.

15
00:00:46,325 --> 00:00:49,999
Within a month, a gang headquarters had been destroyed

16
00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:53,694
from the air, a national stadium had changed hands,

17
00:00:53,714 --> 00:00:56,568
and Haiti's justice minister had toured CECOT.

18
00:00:57,888 --> 00:00:59,886
But one thing had not happened.

19
00:00:59,906 --> 00:01:02,240
The four men had not come home.

20
00:01:04,980 --> 00:01:07,707
Chapter 1. Before the storm.

21
00:01:12,307 --> 00:01:15,806
El Salvador's soldiers did not arrive in Haiti in

22
00:01:15,826 --> 00:01:19,325
twenty twenty six. They had been there for almost

23
00:01:19,345 --> 00:01:20,108
two years.

24
00:01:21,428 --> 00:01:23,395
In January twenty twenty five,

25
00:01:23,415 --> 00:01:26,974
eight members of the Salvadoran Air Force landed in

26
00:01:26,994 --> 00:01:29,757
Port au Prince, in non combat roles,

27
00:01:29,777 --> 00:01:32,540
to support the Kenyan led police mission.

28
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:35,323
A month later, about seventy more followed.

29
00:01:36,643 --> 00:01:39,498
Their job was in the air.

30
00:01:39,518 --> 00:01:43,811
Salvadoran helicopters flew medical evacuations and moved personnel over

31
00:01:43,831 --> 00:01:48,124
a capital where many roads belonged to the gangs.

32
00:01:49,444 --> 00:01:51,105
In twenty twenty five,

33
00:01:51,125 --> 00:01:54,888
the UN Security Council turned the Kenyan mission into

34
00:01:54,908 --> 00:01:57,410
something larger, the Gang Suppression Force.

35
00:01:57,430 --> 00:02:01,193
It was planned at five thousand five hundred personnel.

36
00:02:01,213 --> 00:02:02,875
In twenty twenty six,

37
00:02:02,895 --> 00:02:06,238
according to reports, it had around fifteen hundred.

38
00:02:07,558 --> 00:02:10,773
By the end of September twenty twenty six,

39
00:02:10,793 --> 00:02:14,413
El Salvador had at least one hundred and twenty

40
00:02:14,433 --> 00:02:16,031
four people in Haiti.

41
00:02:16,051 --> 00:02:19,671
Its Legislative Assembly had just extended their mission for

42
00:02:19,691 --> 00:02:22,502
another year. It looked like a quiet,

43
00:02:22,522 --> 00:02:25,333
technical contribution. It did not stay quiet.

44
00:02:27,673 --> 00:02:29,982
Chapter 2. The ambush.

45
00:02:34,582 --> 00:02:38,685
On October eighteenth, four Salvadoran aviation technicians left their

46
00:02:38,705 --> 00:02:41,892
base. According to reports in El Salvador,

47
00:02:41,912 --> 00:02:46,015
they had visited a market in what Haitians call

48
00:02:46,035 --> 00:02:50,138
a red zone, an area controlled by armed groups.

49
00:02:51,458 --> 00:02:53,401
Near the village of Santo,

50
00:02:53,421 --> 00:02:56,148
in the commune of Croix des Bouquets,

51
00:02:56,168 --> 00:02:58,110
their armored vehicle was attacked.

52
00:02:58,130 --> 00:03:00,073
It was destroyed by fire.

53
00:03:00,093 --> 00:03:02,035
The men escaped the vehicle,

54
00:03:02,055 --> 00:03:03,213
and were captured.

55
00:03:04,533 --> 00:03:08,079
An analyst from the International Crisis Group said the

56
00:03:08,099 --> 00:03:10,457
technicians had not had adequate security.

57
00:03:10,477 --> 00:03:14,024
The next day, a Salvadoran helicopter searching for them

58
00:03:14,044 --> 00:03:15,213
was shot at.

59
00:03:16,533 --> 00:03:18,146
Who took them? Officially,

60
00:03:18,166 --> 00:03:19,779
no group was identified,

61
00:03:19,799 --> 00:03:22,229
and no group claimed the attack.

62
00:03:22,249 --> 00:03:25,904
Some Haitian outlets said the men were being held

63
00:03:25,924 --> 00:03:28,354
by a gang called Chèn Méchan.

64
00:03:28,374 --> 00:03:32,029
The area is close to the territory of one

65
00:03:32,049 --> 00:03:34,070
of Haiti's most feared gangs,

66
00:03:34,090 --> 00:03:35,295
four hundred Mawozo.

67
00:03:36,615 --> 00:03:39,662
Days later, the leader of four hundred Mawozo,

68
00:03:39,682 --> 00:03:41,578
Wilson Joseph, posted a video.

69
00:03:41,598 --> 00:03:43,111
He denied any role.

70
00:03:43,131 --> 00:03:46,561
He said Chèn Méchan had fired on the vehicle

71
00:03:46,581 --> 00:03:50,011
by mistake, and that he himself would have taken

72
00:03:50,031 --> 00:03:53,460
the men alive. It is the claim of a

73
00:03:53,480 --> 00:03:56,910
gang leader, and it has not been independently confirmed.

74
00:03:59,250 --> 00:04:01,884
Chapter 3. The promise.

75
00:04:06,484 --> 00:04:08,003
On October twenty first,

76
00:04:08,023 --> 00:04:11,467
President Nayib Bukele wrote on X that his men

77
00:04:11,487 --> 00:04:13,006
were being held hostage,

78
00:04:13,026 --> 00:04:16,084
and that the mission now had one goal.

79
00:04:16,104 --> 00:04:18,778
To bring them back alive and unharmed.

80
00:04:20,098 --> 00:04:21,756
If that failed, he said,

81
00:04:21,776 --> 00:04:23,770
El Salvador would finish the gangs,

82
00:04:23,790 --> 00:04:26,119
just as it had done at home.

83
00:04:26,139 --> 00:04:29,140
For a man whose prisons hold tens of thousands

84
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:30,482
of accused gang members,

85
00:04:30,502 --> 00:04:32,496
it was not an empty phrase.

86
00:04:33,816 --> 00:04:37,027
Haiti's prime minister, Alix Didier Fils Aimé,

87
00:04:37,047 --> 00:04:41,182
called the release of the four men an absolute

88
00:04:41,202 --> 00:04:41,644
priority.

89
00:04:42,964 --> 00:04:44,899
Haiti's gangs answered on video.

90
00:04:44,919 --> 00:04:47,637
A gang leader known as Krisla said,

91
00:04:47,657 --> 00:04:50,374
we didn't ask Bukele to come here.

92
00:04:50,394 --> 00:04:53,893
Wilson Joseph said he would wait for the Salvadorans,

93
00:04:53,913 --> 00:04:56,240
and that he would not run.

94
00:04:57,560 --> 00:05:01,015
Then came the darkest moment of the first week.

95
00:05:01,035 --> 00:05:03,331
According to the New York Times,

96
00:05:03,351 --> 00:05:04,876
burned bodies were recovered,

97
00:05:04,896 --> 00:05:07,192
and work began to identify them.

98
00:05:07,212 --> 00:05:10,281
Bukele said the bodies were not his men.

99
00:05:10,301 --> 00:05:13,756
The accounts of exactly how the bodies were found

100
00:05:13,776 --> 00:05:15,301
do not fully agree.

101
00:05:17,641 --> 00:05:19,973
Chapter 4. The arrival.

102
00:05:24,573 --> 00:05:28,093
The first special forces arrived around October twenty second.

103
00:05:28,113 --> 00:05:30,453
According to the Wall Street Journal,

104
00:05:30,473 --> 00:05:32,420
about one hundred of them.

105
00:05:33,740 --> 00:05:36,495
They kept coming. On October twenty seventh,

106
00:05:36,515 --> 00:05:40,063
a source told Reuters that about one thousand Salvadoran

107
00:05:40,083 --> 00:05:42,442
troops had deployed. The next day,

108
00:05:42,462 --> 00:05:46,010
El Salvador's foreign ministry said the number was two

109
00:05:46,030 --> 00:05:49,578
thousand. That is more soldiers than the entire UN

110
00:05:49,598 --> 00:05:51,957
backed force had in the country.

111
00:05:53,277 --> 00:05:57,411
American military aircraft and Colombian Air Force planes helped

112
00:05:57,431 --> 00:06:01,565
fly them in. The Dominican Republic helped with logistics.

113
00:06:02,885 --> 00:06:05,593
According to reports, Donald Trump told Bukele,

114
00:06:05,613 --> 00:06:07,932
do what you have to do.

115
00:06:07,952 --> 00:06:11,440
Bukele said El Salvador was paying ninety percent of

116
00:06:11,460 --> 00:06:14,558
the cost. He did not give a total.

117
00:06:15,878 --> 00:06:18,291
And here is the unusual part.

118
00:06:18,311 --> 00:06:21,939
Most of these soldiers were not under the UN.

119
00:06:21,959 --> 00:06:25,588
A UN spokesman said most Salvadoran troops were outside

120
00:06:25,608 --> 00:06:27,210
the Gang Suppression Force,

121
00:06:27,230 --> 00:06:30,858
and that the deployment was a bilateral matter between

122
00:06:30,878 --> 00:06:32,480
El Salvador and Haiti.

123
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:34,507
According to the Miami Herald,

124
00:06:34,527 --> 00:06:36,939
they answered to a Salvadoran colonel.

125
00:06:38,259 --> 00:06:40,718
At home, the mission was popular.

126
00:06:40,738 --> 00:06:44,435
In a CID Gallup poll taken in late October,

127
00:06:44,455 --> 00:06:48,153
eighty six percent of Salvadorans approved of the rescue

128
00:06:48,173 --> 00:06:51,870
mission. Eighty two percent said they were worried about

129
00:06:51,890 --> 00:06:52,696
the risks.

130
00:06:54,836 --> 00:06:58,004
Chapter 5. The first operations.

131
00:07:02,604 --> 00:07:06,452
On October thirtieth, Salvadoran troops began their first patrols,

132
00:07:06,472 --> 00:07:08,602
in Tabarre, near the U.S.

133
00:07:08,622 --> 00:07:11,610
embassy, where they set up a base.

134
00:07:11,630 --> 00:07:15,049
The next day, gunfire hit a convoy nearby.

135
00:07:16,369 --> 00:07:19,903
On November second, Salvadoran armored vehicles pushed into the

136
00:07:19,923 --> 00:07:21,877
Plaine du Cul de Sac,

137
00:07:21,897 --> 00:07:24,642
the plain north east of the capital,

138
00:07:24,662 --> 00:07:27,011
the heartland of four hundred Mawozo.

139
00:07:27,031 --> 00:07:29,775
According to the Spanish news agency EFE,

140
00:07:29,795 --> 00:07:32,935
at least a dozen gang members were killed.

141
00:07:34,255 --> 00:07:36,898
Not everyone in Haiti welcomed them.

142
00:07:36,918 --> 00:07:39,562
The same day, according to EFE,

143
00:07:39,582 --> 00:07:43,557
people in some neighborhoods were forced into protests against

144
00:07:43,577 --> 00:07:47,553
the intervention, under death threats from the gang alliance

145
00:07:47,573 --> 00:07:48,441
Viv Ansanm.

146
00:07:49,761 --> 00:07:53,013
And the fighting had a cost for ordinary people.

147
00:07:53,033 --> 00:07:56,286
Doctors Without Borders said it treated thirty civilians wounded

148
00:07:56,306 --> 00:07:59,558
by gunfire or explosions in just the first week

149
00:07:59,578 --> 00:08:00,649
after the ambush.

150
00:08:01,969 --> 00:08:04,253
A Haitian group, UNA Haiti,

151
00:08:04,273 --> 00:08:07,017
wrote to the UN Secretary General.

152
00:08:07,037 --> 00:08:11,163
It alleged that aerial bombardments and helicopter attacks had

153
00:08:11,183 --> 00:08:13,927
killed civilians in Croix des Bouquets,

154
00:08:13,947 --> 00:08:16,691
and it asked for an investigation.

155
00:08:16,711 --> 00:08:20,377
Bukele denied that his forces had dropped bombs.

156
00:08:21,697 --> 00:08:24,786
We're following the Haiti story as it unfolds.

157
00:08:24,806 --> 00:08:27,895
Subscribe, so you don't miss the next chapter.

158
00:08:30,235 --> 00:08:32,637
Chapter 6. Friction.

159
00:08:37,237 --> 00:08:39,610
Haiti's government stood behind the operation.

160
00:08:39,630 --> 00:08:43,200
On November third, the prime minister said the Salvadoran

161
00:08:43,220 --> 00:08:46,790
troops were not there to replace the Haitian state.

162
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:49,867
Washington was less comfortable.

163
00:08:49,887 --> 00:08:52,532
According to reports, on November fourth,

164
00:08:52,552 --> 00:08:56,529
the top U.S. diplomat in Haiti asked the prime

165
00:08:56,549 --> 00:09:00,526
minister to halt the operation until the Salvadorans coordinated

166
00:09:00,546 --> 00:09:02,747
with the UN backed force.

167
00:09:02,767 --> 00:09:06,744
The next day, the embassy complained about a lack

168
00:09:06,764 --> 00:09:10,742
of coordination. El Salvador's foreign minister said the forces

169
00:09:10,762 --> 00:09:12,074
were already coordinating.

170
00:09:13,394 --> 00:09:14,770
Bukele answered in public.

171
00:09:14,790 --> 00:09:17,912
Trump told me to do what we have to

172
00:09:17,932 --> 00:09:21,054
do, he said, and now a bureaucrat is opposing

173
00:09:21,074 --> 00:09:21,403
it?

174
00:09:22,723 --> 00:09:24,467
There was another dispute.

175
00:09:24,487 --> 00:09:28,434
The American diplomat reported that three Salvadoran soldiers had

176
00:09:28,454 --> 00:09:31,079
been injured. El Salvador denied it,

177
00:09:31,099 --> 00:09:34,165
and accused him of spreading false information.

178
00:09:36,505 --> 00:09:39,185
Chapter 7. From the sky.

179
00:09:43,785 --> 00:09:46,980
In early November, the war over Port au Prince

180
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,409
moved into the air.

181
00:09:49,729 --> 00:09:52,020
In Cité Soleil, Mathias Saintil,

182
00:09:52,040 --> 00:09:55,256
the leader of a gang called Boston,

183
00:09:55,276 --> 00:09:58,029
was killed by a loitering munition,

184
00:09:58,049 --> 00:10:01,265
a drone that dives onto its target.

185
00:10:01,285 --> 00:10:04,962
According to reports, the operation involved Haitian police,

186
00:10:04,982 --> 00:10:06,811
the UN backed force,

187
00:10:06,831 --> 00:10:10,971
El Salvador, and a private contractor linked to the

188
00:10:10,991 --> 00:10:12,820
American businessman Erik Prince.

189
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:17,463
Then Bukele did something no head of state usually

190
00:10:17,483 --> 00:10:20,434
does in public. According to the Associated Press,

191
00:10:20,454 --> 00:10:23,776
he asked people on X to help identify the

192
00:10:23,796 --> 00:10:25,262
home of Wilson Joseph,

193
00:10:25,282 --> 00:10:27,490
so that he could destroy it.

194
00:10:28,810 --> 00:10:32,729
On November eighth, Salvadoran helicopters and a loitering munition

195
00:10:32,749 --> 00:10:35,354
struck a house linked to Joseph,

196
00:10:35,374 --> 00:10:38,855
described as the headquarters of four hundred Mawozo.

197
00:10:38,875 --> 00:10:41,043
According to the Miami Herald,

198
00:10:41,063 --> 00:10:44,107
up to twenty gang members were killed.

199
00:10:44,127 --> 00:10:48,045
Two days later, Bukele confirmed the headquarters had been

200
00:10:48,065 --> 00:10:48,483
destroyed.

201
00:10:49,803 --> 00:10:52,393
Four hundred Mawozo changed its tone.

202
00:10:52,413 --> 00:10:55,874
Joseph had already asked the UN to mediate.

203
00:10:55,894 --> 00:10:59,790
A spokesperson told the Associated Press the gang was

204
00:10:59,810 --> 00:11:01,965
ready to negotiate and disarm,

205
00:11:01,985 --> 00:11:03,705
if international interference ended.

206
00:11:05,025 --> 00:11:07,170
El Salvador's vice president,

207
00:11:07,190 --> 00:11:12,041
Félix Ulloa, called UN mediation with the gangs unacceptable.

208
00:11:13,961 --> 00:11:17,975
On November eighteenth, Salvadoran helicopters destroyed a house in

209
00:11:17,995 --> 00:11:20,216
Canaan belonging to Jeff Larose,

210
00:11:20,236 --> 00:11:23,353
the leader of a gang called Taliban.

211
00:11:23,373 --> 00:11:26,043
Whether he was inside is unknown.

212
00:11:26,063 --> 00:11:28,284
According to the Associated Press,

213
00:11:28,304 --> 00:11:31,869
the UN backed force did not take part.

214
00:11:34,209 --> 00:11:36,657
Chapter 8. The stadium.

215
00:11:41,257 --> 00:11:45,006
In the middle of Port au Prince stands the

216
00:11:45,026 --> 00:11:47,518
Sylvio Cator stadium, Haiti's national stadium.

217
00:11:47,538 --> 00:11:49,193
Since twenty twenty four,

218
00:11:49,213 --> 00:11:51,705
it had been in gang territory.

219
00:11:53,025 --> 00:11:55,581
Around November twelfth, according to reports,

220
00:11:55,601 --> 00:11:59,017
Salvadoran troops set up a base inside it.

221
00:11:59,037 --> 00:12:02,881
Bukele told the gangs to leave the area around

222
00:12:02,901 --> 00:12:05,458
the stadium, or face the consequences.

223
00:12:06,778 --> 00:12:09,977
For many Haitians, after years of fear,

224
00:12:09,997 --> 00:12:11,816
it was a symbol.

225
00:12:11,836 --> 00:12:15,955
On November seventeenth, thousands marched in support of the

226
00:12:15,975 --> 00:12:18,254
intervention, in Port au Prince,

227
00:12:18,274 --> 00:12:20,093
Kenscoff, Jérémie and Belladère.

228
00:12:21,413 --> 00:12:26,186
In El Salvador, the opposition was less enthusiastic.

229
00:12:26,206 --> 00:12:29,780
The opposition party FMLN's presidential candidate,

230
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:33,974
Rafael Aguirre, called it an unnecessary war.

231
00:12:36,314 --> 00:12:38,692
Chapter 9. The cost.

232
00:12:43,292 --> 00:12:45,421
How many people have died?

233
00:12:45,441 --> 00:12:47,999
According to the conflict monitor ACLED,

234
00:12:48,019 --> 00:12:51,866
by November eleventh more than one hundred people had

235
00:12:51,886 --> 00:12:54,014
been killed in the intervention.

236
00:12:54,034 --> 00:12:57,451
At least twenty six of them were civilians.

237
00:12:57,471 --> 00:12:59,170
Other counts are lower.

238
00:12:59,190 --> 00:13:01,319
The numbers are still disputed.

239
00:13:02,639 --> 00:13:06,347
Amnesty International urged both governments to make the terms

240
00:13:06,367 --> 00:13:08,004
of the deployment public.

241
00:13:08,024 --> 00:13:11,733
El Salvador's vice president said the terms would not

242
00:13:11,753 --> 00:13:14,219
be disclosed until diplomatic conditions allowed,

243
00:13:14,239 --> 00:13:16,290
and called the deployment legitimate.

244
00:13:17,610 --> 00:13:21,114
An ACLED researcher warned that operations running in parallel

245
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:24,638
to the UN backed force could undermine its legitimacy.

246
00:13:25,958 --> 00:13:27,715
And on November twentieth,

247
00:13:27,735 --> 00:13:30,381
El Salvador paid its own price.

248
00:13:30,401 --> 00:13:34,380
According to reports, three Salvadoran soldiers were killed and

249
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:38,379
one was injured, when explosives they were handling detonated.

250
00:13:40,919 --> 00:13:43,832
Chapter 10. A CECOT for Haiti?

251
00:13:48,432 --> 00:13:50,233
In March twenty twenty four,

252
00:13:50,253 --> 00:13:53,512
as we showed in part one of this series,

253
00:13:53,532 --> 00:13:56,791
Haiti's two largest prisons were emptied in a single

254
00:13:56,811 --> 00:14:00,071
night. More than four thousand seven hundred prisoners walked

255
00:14:00,091 --> 00:14:00,435
out.

256
00:14:01,755 --> 00:14:04,166
In November twenty twenty six,

257
00:14:04,186 --> 00:14:06,597
Haiti's justice minister, Patrick Pélissier,

258
00:14:06,617 --> 00:14:08,542
travelled to El Salvador,

259
00:14:08,562 --> 00:14:12,918
and toured CECOT, the mega prison built for forty

260
00:14:12,938 --> 00:14:13,891
thousand men.

261
00:14:15,211 --> 00:14:18,749
On November twentieth, he announced that Haiti and El

262
00:14:18,769 --> 00:14:22,307
Salvador would build three new prisons for gang members.

263
00:14:22,327 --> 00:14:24,679
Where, how much they would cost,

264
00:14:24,699 --> 00:14:26,260
and who would pay,

265
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:27,446
was not announced.

